[%# SM1295 (#340): built-in Odoo sign-in component - the ready-made /odoo-signin
    page's (SM1160's site sign-in). Use on a page:
      ::: odoo-signin
      :::
    The button opens the Odoo sign-in dialog (password, then the authenticator code
    where Odoo asks) through /assets/lazysite-odoo.js, which the processor adds for
    any page carrying data-ls-odoo-*; once signed in, it goes to the page's ?next=
    when that is a path on this site and to / otherwise (data-ls-odoo-next, SM1299;
    the endpoint decides the path), and a person already signed in sees who, with
    a sign-out that ends the Odoo session too. No inline style: the form classes
    are styled by the fallback chrome and the base form rules. A layout may override it, keeping the data-ls-odoo-* attributes.
    ONE LINE ON PURPOSE: the page's Markdown pass ends an HTML block early on an
    indented or repeated tag and wraps the rest in <p>, which split this markup. -%]
<section class="lz-odoo-signin"><div class="lazysite-form" data-ls-odoo-out><p class="form-field form-submit"><button type="button" data-ls-odoo-signin data-ls-odoo-next>Sign in with your Odoo login</button></p></div><p class="lz-odoo-signed-in" data-ls-odoo-in hidden>Signed in as <strong data-ls-odoo-name></strong>. <a href="/">Go to the site</a> &middot; <a href="#" data-ls-odoo-signout>Sign out</a></p><noscript><p>Signing in needs JavaScript in your browser.</p></noscript></section>
